---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '@/utils/content';

const title = `Work · ${site.name}`;
const description =
  'Content samples: long-form articles, campaign work, social strategy, and community — all from Rocket and DhiWise.';
---

<Base {title} {description} ogImage="/og/work.png">
  <div class="container" style="padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);">

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-16">
      <span class="section-label">Work</span>
      <h1 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);">
        Writing, campaigns,<br />and community.
      </h1>
      <p class="rh-body" style="max-width: 34rem;">
        Five years of content strategy, technical writing, and community building at
        Rocket (rocket.new, formerly DhiWise). Only facts from published, bylined work.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Long-form writing -->
    <section aria-labelledby="longform-heading" class="mb-16">
      <h2 id="longform-heading" class="section-title" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">
        <span class="section-label">Long-form</span>
        Technical essays and articles
      </h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 mt-6">

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">Original essay · Oct 2026</span>
          <a href="/writing/essay" class="sample-title">
            The output is free now. Hire for the judgment.
          </a>
          <p class="sample-body">
            When AI makes the output cheap, the scarce thing becomes knowing whether
            the output is right — and what to do when it isn't. Written from real
            experience rebuilding Rocket's Instagram and growing the Discord from
            zero. About 1,250 words. Every source cited.
          </p>
          <a href="/writing/essay" class="rh-artifact">Read →</a>
        </article>

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">Published on rocket.new · 30 Sep 2026 · ~2,150 words</span>
          <a
            href="https://rocket.new/blog/htmx-vs-react"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="sample-title"
          >
            HTMX vs React (2026): Comparison Table, Checklist and When to Use Each
          </a>
          <p class="sample-body">
            "Why is every second dev thread now questioning whether React is overkill
            for most web pages?" Opens on a real engineering-culture argument, takes a
            position, and gives a decision framework that works for both an engineer
            and a founder.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://rocket.new/blog/htmx-vs-react"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="rh-artifact"
          >
            Read on rocket.new →
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">Published on rocket.new · 30 Sep 2026 · ~2,200 words</span>
          <a
            href="https://rocket.new/blog/linear-mcp-server-how-to-connect-issue-tracker"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="sample-title"
          >
            Linear MCP Server: How to Connect Your Issue Tracker to AI
          </a>
          <p class="sample-body">
            Explains the Model Context Protocol plainly and accurately, gets the
            OAuth and transport details right, and lands the concept for both a
            developer and a product manager. Part of the 144 bylines on AI agents
            and agentic tooling.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://rocket.new/blog/linear-mcp-server-how-to-connect-issue-tracker"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="rh-artifact"
          >
            Read on rocket.new →
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">All 144 articles</span>
          <a
            href="https://rocket.new/author/rakesh-purohit"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="sample-title"
          >
            rocket.new/author/rakesh-purohit
          </a>
          <p class="sample-body">
            AI agents, MCP servers, framework trade-offs, SEO and AEO content built
            to be cited by LLMs. Also on
            <a href="https://dhiwise.com/author/rakesh-purohit" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DhiWise</a> and
            <a href="https://therakeshpurohit.medium.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medium</a>.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://rocket.new/author/rakesh-purohit"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="rh-artifact"
          >
            All articles →
          </a>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Short posts -->
    <section aria-labelledby="shortform-heading" class="mb-16">
      <h2 id="shortform-heading" class="section-title" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">
        <span class="section-label">Short posts</span>
        X (Twitter)
      </h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 mt-6">

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">X · 8 Sep 2026</span>
          <a
            href="https://x.com/iRakeshPurohit/status/2097339427336896910"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="sample-title"
          >
            Headroom — context compression for AI agents
          </a>
          <p class="sample-body">
            "Former Netflix engineer Tejas Chopra open-sourced Headroom, a local
            context-compression layer for AI agents... One example cut 10,144 tokens
            to 1,260 while preserving the same critical error." Hook on a credible
            person, concrete numbers, one vivid proof point.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://x.com/iRakeshPurohit/status/2097339427336896910"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="rh-artifact"
          >
            Read on X →
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">X · 10 Sep 2026</span>
          <a
            href="https://x.com/iRakeshPurohit/status/2098061684510474241"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="sample-title"
          >
            ffmpeg-skill — a local video editor for coding agents
          </a>
          <p class="sample-body">
            "The useful part is the workflow." Skips the feature list and lands on
            the one detail that matters: the agent probes the actual file first,
            avoids re-encoding when possible, dry-runs the plan, then verifies the
            output. Taste as an editorial move.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://x.com/iRakeshPurohit/status/2098061684510474241"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="rh-artifact"
          >
            Read on X →
          </a>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Campaigns and community -->
    <section aria-labelledby="campaigns-heading" class="mb-16">
      <h2 id="campaigns-heading" class="section-title" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">
        <span class="section-label">Campaigns &amp; community</span>
        Strategy and operations
      </h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 mt-6">

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">Campaign</span>
          <p class="sample-title" style="cursor: default;">30Days30Usecases</p>
          <p class="sample-body">
            Project lead for a 30-day content campaign. 10 direct reports over
            2 months. One published use case per day, each technically accurate
            and audience-tested in Discord before shipping.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">Social · @rocketdotnew</span>
          <p class="sample-title" style="cursor: default;">Instagram strategy rebuild</p>
          <p class="sample-body">
            Rebuilt Rocket's Instagram strategy from the audience up. Posts went from
            ~3 likes (mostly internal) to up to ~10k engagements per carousel.
            Then planned the shift to Reels for short-form video.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="sample-card reveal">
          <span class="sample-type">Community</span>
          <p class="sample-title" style="cursor: default;">Discord: 0 → 22k</p>
          <p class="sample-body">
            Grew the Rocket developer Discord from 0 to 22,000 members. Used as a
            direct line to how developers react to the product and the content.
            Also manages @rocketdotnew on X and contributes to long-form YouTube.
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Engineering note -->
    <section aria-labelledby="engineering-heading">
      <h2 id="engineering-heading" class="section-title" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">
        <span class="section-label">Why the tech is right</span>
        Engineering work at Rocket
      </h2>
      <div class="rh-layout mt-6">
        <div>
          <p class="rh-body">
            The writing is grounded in real engineering. He's not writing about
            tools he hasn't used — he's shipped the Figma plugin with 100K+ users,
            architected the Webflow-to-Next.js migration, served 1M+ monthly users
            on a $70 infrastructure budget, and built the Gen-AI content workflow
            that saves 20 developer hours a month.
          </p>
          <p class="rh-body" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
            When he writes that MCP reduces context overhead or that ISR improves
            SEO indexing time to two days, he's written it because he measured it.
            That's the whole trick.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rh-margin-note">
          1M+ monthly users<br />$70 infra budget<br />Vercel edge<br />Core Web Vitals: 91/88
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</Base>
